command Rose.Core.Login
  : Screens.Console, Caps.Create_Endpoint, Time.Timer_Service
  with Summary     => "Log a user in at the console.",
       Description => """
          Login asks for a user name and a password at the console, and
          checks them with Auth (#457). For the right password, it
          completes, and gives the user's User interface; the console
          supervisor runs the session (#526). For a wrong one, it waits
          a few seconds, says that the login failed, and asks again.

          It is transient (#524): no checkpoint saves it, so the password
          it reads never reaches the disk from its memory, and a restore
          never brings back a login that was half done. Its launcher's
          call to it fails at a restore, and the supervisor launches it
          again.
          """,
       Live,
       Transient
is
   Auth : in Users.Auth
     with Help => "the Auth interface, which checks a user's password";
   User : out Users.User
     with Help => "the user who logged in";
end Rose.Core.Login;
